4. Reread the SOURCE DISCIPLINE block of `prompts/article-prompt.md`
   against your own draft: every textual claim traceable to a ledger
   unit; every claim resting only on the commentary's say-so, not the
   primary text, marked as such; every argumentative step you could
   not support marked `[UNSUPPORTED — needs X]` rather than smoothed
   over.

Change only `synthesis/outputs/intentionalitaet-article-draft.md` and
`synthesis/gaps.json`. Do not hand-edit the generated ledger, do not
touch the extraction or inheritance records, and do not move anything
into `commentaries/` or `articles/` — publishing this draft, if it's
good enough to publish, is a separate decision for afterward. Do not
commit to `main`. If you have to commit to hand the work back, use a
new branch.

Finish with a short report: the thesis you argued, the gap ids you
raised or cited, and the checker's final output.
